#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exercise"
msgstr "Ejercicio"

#. type: \t; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "See also"
msgstr "Ver también"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "<a cbot>Programming</a>, <a cbot|type>types</a> and <a cbot|category>categories</a>."
msgstr "<a cbot>Programación</a>, <a cbot|type>tipos</a> y <a cbot|category>categorías</a>."

#. type: Title-text
#: ../scene.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Massacre"
msgstr "Matanza"

#. type: Resume-text
#: ../scene.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use a loop in order to destroy six targets."
msgstr "Usa un bucle para destruir seis objetivos."

#. type: ScriptName-text
#: ../scene.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Go"
msgstr "Ir"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Destroy the six <a object|bottarg>targets</a> with a program using a loop. The bot must move 5m forward to get from one target to the next."
msgstr "Destruye los seis <a object|bottarg>objetivos</a> con un programa usando un bucle. El bot debe avanzar 5m para pasar de un objetivo a otro."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "General principle"
msgstr "Principio general"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The program must execute the following scheme:\n"
"Repeat 6 times :"
msgstr ""
"El programa debe ejecutar el siguiente esquema:\n"
"Repite 6 veces:"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "move 5m forward"
msgstr "avanzar 5m"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "turn 90 degrees left"
msgstr "girar 90 grados a la izquierda"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "shoot"
msgstr "disparar"

#. type: Bullet: 'o'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "turn 90 degrees right"
msgstr "girar 90 grados a la derecha"

#. type: Image filename
#: ../help/help.E.txt:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "tfor1"
msgstr "tfor1"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instruction <code>for ( )</code>"
msgstr "Instrucción <code>for ( )</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "The instruction <code><a cbot|for>for</a></code> asks for 3 expressions:"
msgstr "La instrucción <code><a cbot|for>for</a></code> pide 3 expresiones:"

#. type: Bullet: '1)'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize the counting variable."
msgstr "Inicializar la variable de conteo."

#. type: Bullet: '2)'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "The end <a cbot|cond>condition</a>."
msgstr "La condición de <a cbot|cond>fin</a>."

#. type: Bullet: '3)'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "The counting <a cbot|expr>expression</a>."
msgstr "La <a cbot|expr>expresión</a> de conteo."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is the loop once it is integrated into the program frame:"
msgstr "Aquí está el bucle una vez integrado en el marco del programa:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<c/>extern void object::Massacre( )\n"
"{\n"
"\tfor ( int i=0 ; i<6 ; i=i+1 )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\t<n/>instructions repeated 6 times ...<c/>\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"<c/>extern void object::Massacre( )\n"
"{\n"
"\tfor ( int i=0 ; i<6 ; i=i+1 )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\t<n/>instrucciones repetidas 6 veces ...<c/>\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "ATTENTION: The line <code>for ( )</code> must not be followed by a <a cbot|term>semicolon</a> !"
msgstr "ATENCIÓN: La línea <code>for ( )</code> no debe ser seguida por un <a cbot|term>punto y coma</a> !"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explanation of the instruction <code>for ( )</code>"
msgstr "Explicación de la instrucción <code>for ( )</code>"

#. type: Bullet: '1)'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>int i=0</code>"
msgstr "<code>int i=0</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "    The <a cbot|var>variable</a> i is set to zero before the beginning of the loop."
msgstr "    La <a cbot|var>variable</a> i se establece en cero antes del inicio del bucle."

#. type: Bullet: '2)'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>i<6</code>"
msgstr "<code>i<6</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "    The loop will be executed as long as i is smaller than 6."
msgstr "    El bucle se ejecutará siempre que i sea menor que 6."

#. type: Bullet: '3)'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "<code>i=i+1</code>"
msgstr "<code>i=i+1</code>"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "    At the end of every loop, add 1 to the variable i."
msgstr "    Al final de cada bucle, añade 1 a la variable i."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blocks"
msgstr "Bloques"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use braces <code>{ }</code> in order to create a <a cbot|bloc>block</a>. All the instructions that must be executed in the <code>for</code> loop are held together by a block. The whole program itself is made up of a block:"
msgstr "Usa llaves <code>{ }</code> para crear un <a cbot|bloc>bloque</a>. Todas las instrucciones que deben ejecutarse en el bucle <code>for</code> se mantienen juntas en un bloque. Todo el programa en sí está compuesto por un bloque:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"extern void object::massacre( )\n"
"{\n"
"\t<n/>fill in here ...<c/>\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"extern void object::massacre( )\n"
"{\n"
"\t<n/>rellena aquí ...<c/>\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Never change these characters. Just add the instructions of the program between the braces.\n"
"You can fit several blocks one into the other. For example the <code>for</code> block is fitted into the block of the whole program. In order to improve readability, the editor lines up the braces belonging to the different blocks."
msgstr ""
"Nunca cambies estos caracteres. Solo añade las instrucciones del programa entre las llaves.\n"
"Puedes meter varios bloques unos dentro de otros. Por ejemplo, el bloque <code>for</code> se mete dentro del bloque de todo el programa. Para mejorar la legibilidad, el editor alinea las llaves que pertenecen a los diferentes bloques."

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember"
msgstr "Recuerda"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:52
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The instruction used to move forward is <c/><a cbot|move>move</a>();<n/>.\n"
"The instruction used to turn the bot is <c/><a cbot|turn>turn</a>();<n/>. A positive angle turns left.\n"
"The instruction used to fire the cannon is <c/><a cbot|fire>fire</a>(1);<n/>. A one-second burst allows to destroy all six <a object|bottarg>targets</a>."
msgstr ""
"La instrucción usada para avanzar es <c/><a cbot|move>move</a>();<n/>.\n"
"La instrucción usada para girar el bot es <c/><a cbot|turn>turn</a>();<n/>. Un ángulo positivo gira a la izquierda.\n"
"La instrucción usada para disparar el cañón es <c/><a cbot|fire>fire</a>(1);<n/>. Una ráfaga de un segundo permite destruir los seis <a object|bottarg>objetivos</a>."
